NAME
    rusagedemo - what times(2) and getrusage(2) report

SYNOPSIS
    rusagedemo

DESCRIPTION
    Forks once and prints the caller's CPU-time accounting from
    times(2) and getrusage(2), for the process itself and for the
    child it waited for. The child burns a few ticks of the 100 Hz
    scheduler clock in a busy loop and exits with status 7; the
    kernel folds its time into the parent's tms_cutime and into
    getrusage(RUSAGE_CHILDREN) at the exit, which is what the demo
    then shows. Every line printed is a claim about the accounting
    the kernel does, so this doubles as the regression test for the
    two syscalls.

    VNU executes all code at privilege 0 with per-process page tables
    and does not sample a privilege level, so user and system time
    are not separated the way Linux separates them: every tick a
    process runs is charged to utime, and stime/cstime are always 0
    (see ABI.md and <vnu/abi.h>). The demo prints those zeros rather
    than hiding them. getrusage's unmeasurable fields (maxrss, page
    faults, block I/O, ...) are likewise reported as 0.

EXIT STATUS
    0 when the child burned its ticks and was reaped with status 7;
    1 when fork() or waitpid() misbehaved.

SEE ALSO
    times(2), getrusage(2), forkdemo(1), ttytest(1), man(1)
